<article class="env-lemma" id="02Y5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02Y5">Lemma <span data-tag="02Y5">4.42.1</span>.</a> In the situation above the fibre category of $(\mathcal{C}/U) \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{X}$ over an object $f : V \to U$ of $\mathcal{C}/U$ is the category described as follows: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
objects are pairs $(x, \phi )$, where $x \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{X}_ V)$, and $\phi : f^*y \to F(x)$ is a morphism in $\mathcal{Y}_ V$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the set of morphisms between $(x, \phi )$ and $(x', \phi ')$ is the set of morphisms $\psi : x \to x'$ in $\mathcal{X}_ V$ such that $F(\psi ) = \phi ' \circ \phi ^{-1}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      See discussion above. 
